; A trait method's DEFAULT body can declare its effects, and it was the
; fourth declaration site in a row that could not.
;
; The pattern, four times over: the author tags node A, the compiler
; builds node B from it, and everything downstream checks B. Copying
; the span across is remembered every time; copying word 7 was not.
;
;   expandImplMethods   a written impl method  -> a mangled TAG_D_FN
;   expBuildDecls       a macro template decl  -> an instantiated decl
;   checkImplComplete   a trait DEFAULT        -> a synthesized method
;
; and `attachAxtags` had to learn to descend into each nesting before
; any of them had a tag to lose in the first place.
;
; This one is the oddest of the three because the method is never
; WRITTEN in the impl at all: `(impl (Noisy Int) where ())` defines
; nothing, and `checkImplComplete` synthesizes `Noisy#Int#loud` from
; the trait's default. Measured before the fix: that synthesized
; method drew AX3042 with the tag present and with it absent,
; identically - the tag changed nothing, so no edit could satisfy it.
;
; `quiet` is the control that must FIRE. Same shape, same trait, no
; tag - so it draws AX3042 at its own mangled name. Without it this
; file would assert only that nothing is reported, which a compiler
; that had stopped checking synthesized methods would also satisfy.
(trait (Noisy a) where (
  ;@axiom:effect(io)
  loud :: (-> a Int) = (lambda (x) (__syscall3 1 1 x 0))
  quiet :: (-> a Int) = (lambda (x) (__syscall3 1 1 x 0))
))

(impl (Noisy Int) where ())

(:: caller (-> Int Int))

;@axiom:effect(io)
(fn (caller n) (+ (loud n) (quiet n)))

(:: main Int)

;@axiom:effect(io)
(fn (main) (caller 1))
